1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:04,030
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) The speed limit around residential areas is usually

2
00:00:04,030 --> 00:00:06,050
25 miles per hour.

3
00:00:07,010 --> 00:00:10,530
People usually go above this, except Sarah.

4
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:13,150
Sarah was driving to work.

5
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,210
She turned on the radio.

6
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,650
Her favorite song came on.

7
00:00:18,330 --> 00:00:20,170
She started nodding her head.

8
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:22,530
Then she heard a honk.

9
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:24,330
It came from behind.

10
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,010
A driver wanted to pass her.

11
00:00:27,570 --> 00:00:30,590
She was driving at 25 miles per hour.

12
00:00:31,390 --> 00:00:32,950
He shouldn't be honking.

13
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:35,650
She was following the rules.

14
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:38,130
She started driving slower.

15
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:40,450
He was getting mad.

16
00:00:41,190 --> 00:00:42,510
He kept honking.

17
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:45,210
She drove even slower.

18
00:00:46,090 --> 00:00:48,770
She was now driving 10 miles per hour.

19
00:00:49,610 --> 00:00:51,670
He switched to the right lane.

20
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:54,410
Then he drove, passing her.
